'' A CONVERTING 'operator let' IS NOT THE COPY. Span has a destructor, so a same-type copy
'' is the synthesised 'operator let( byref as const Span )' -- and the only 'let' Span
'' declares takes a double. The call was emitted and the body was not, because ANY written
'' 'let' counted as the copy: 'undefined symbol: SPAN::operator=(SPAN const&)' at the link.
'' fbc prints 42 (fbc-modern 1.20, 2026-09-29).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/implicit-let-converting.bas -o tests/driver/implicitletconv.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/driver/implicitletconv.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  42
